  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Specific Flag Tower of Hanoi: three mapped stepped battered brick terraces, pale pierced parapets/corner posts and bounded supported access flights, tapered octagonal brick shaft with round recessed rosette openings, genuinely open octagonal observation crown/closed roof lip, pole and double-sided red flag/yellow star. Five existing shared brick/stucco/limestone/painted-metal/canvas graphs. No copied inscription, weathering/photo atlas, interior staircase, cafe, military equipment, whole museum or adjacent monument.",
    "identityBasis": "Retained exact-QID OSM way184959290 and standard PMTiles parent35184557048122 with three terrace parts35185232061469/470/471, crown35185232061472 and shaft35185465033114 fix the compound, component outlines and undirected plan axes. Native anchor105.839823532,21.032590491; global heading0 with internal east/south rotation from the first mapped lower-terrace edge. Octagonal shaft/crown phases follow their mapped outlines. Fine gate/stair/facade allocation remains picture-led with25degree/3m uncertainty; no directed surveyed entrance is asserted.",
    "heightBasis": "Mapped terrace tops3.1/6.8/11.9m and shaft30.1m/crown33.4m control height. Commons category distinguishes33.4m masonry from41m including flag; the retained41m fact alone is unqualified. Nominal walk floors2.4/6.1/11.2m reserve0.7m for parapets. Crown openings/roof collars, shaft taper, window/stair inventory, flag shape and footing remain picture/map visualization approximations.",
    "terrainBasis": "Keep original6m standard terrain, paths/water and every independent neighboring building. Replace only the six corresponding parent/terrace/shaft/crown shells. Lowest terrace footing straddles occupied native rim grades; higher terraces and access flights are supported by lower masonry. No ground/water cutout, square flattening or whole museum platform. Coarse terrain and vegetation-obscured pictures do not establish actual foundation engineering.",
